Mesa's Metal WSI on Minkar, without Metal: VK_EXT_metal_surface presents
through CAMetalLayer, whose drawables are IOSurfaces. Every driver takes
the software drivers' path (the image copied to a host-visible buffer,
the CPU copying that into the drawable), after the GPU's copy finishes;
wsi_common_minkar_layer.m stands in for the Metal layer code; BGRA8 only.
RADV lists VK_EXT_metal_surface, and its WSI extensions, where the
platform has it. Chosen when
<Metal/Metal.h> is missing.

